{
  "name": "grayling",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/salmonids.py): a grayling, 40 cm -- slim, a SMALL pointed head with a little UNDERSLUNG mouth; the huge SAIL of a dorsal fin, its base long and its rear the tallest, purple with dark spots in rows and a RED margin (a second narrow sheet); the salmonid's ADIPOSE fin, pelvics under the sail, a forked tail; silver-grey with a violet sheen over rowed scales (`rowscales`), dark lengthwise lines along the scale rows and a few black spots on the fore flank (painted). Each fin is one membrane sheet. A SWIMMER (the fish's plumbing).",
